      "id": "definitions",
      "heading": "Definitions",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "POJO: A simple Java object not bound by any special restriction or requirement (e.g., no need to extend specific classes or implement interfaces).",
            "IoC (Inversion of Control): The design principle where control of object creation and dependency resolution is shifted from the application code to the Spring container.",
            "DI (Dependency Injection): The technique of passing dependencies to objects rather than creating them inside the object."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Spring Boot is an open-source Java-based framework developed by the Pivotal Team. It simplifies the development of new Spring applications with minimal configuration."
        }
      ],
