    {
      "id": "1-choose-the-modules-needed-based-on-application-requirements",
      "heading": "1. Choose the Modules Needed (Based on Application Requirements)",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Spring is modular, so you only need to include the modules relevant to your application to keep it lightweight and efficient. Common scenarios:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Web Application → Add spring-web, spring-webmvc",
            "Database Access → Add spring-jdbc, spring-orm",
            "AOP Functionality → Add spring-aop",
            "Messaging → Add spring-messaging",
            "Testing → Add spring-test"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "blockquote",
          "text": "Tip: Use Maven or Gradle for dependency management. Example (Maven):"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "xml",
          "code": "<dependency>\n  <groupId>org.springframework</groupId>\n  <artifactId>spring-context</artifactId>\n  <version>6.0.8</version>\n</dependency>",
          "runnable": false
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 58,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "2-create-beans-and-configure-them-using-xml-or-annotations",
      "heading": "2. Create Beans and Configure Them Using XML or Annotations",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "In Spring, objects are called beans and are managed by the IoC container."
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "XML-based configuration:"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "xml",
          "code": "<bean id=\"myService\" class=\"com.example.MyService\"/>",
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Annotation-based configuration (preferred in modern applications):"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "java",
          "code": "@Component\npublic class MyService {\n    // Your logic here\n}",
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Then enable component scanning in a config class:"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "java",
          "code": "@Configuration\n@ComponentScan(\"com.example\")\npublic class AppConfig { }",
          "runnable": false
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 29,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "3-set-up-the-applicationcontext",
      "heading": "3. Set Up the ApplicationContext",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The ApplicationContext is the central interface to the Spring IoC container. It instantiates, configures, and assembles beans."
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "XML-based:"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "java",
          "code": "ApplicationContext context = new ClassPathXmlApplicationContext(\"beans.xml\");\nMyService service = context.getBean(MyService.class);",
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Java-based Configuration:"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "java",
          "code": "AnnotationConfigApplicationContext context = new AnnotationConfigApplicationContext(AppConfig.class);\nMyService service = context.getBean(MyService.class);",
          "runnable": false
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 20,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "4-leverage-dependency-injection-di",
      "heading": "4. Leverage Dependency Injection (DI)",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Spring handles injection of dependencies, reducing tight coupling between components."
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Constructor-based Injection:"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "java",
          "code": "@Component\npublic class OrderService {\n    private final PaymentService paymentService;\n\n    @Autowired\n    public OrderService(PaymentService paymentService) {\n        this.paymentService = paymentService;\n    }\n}",
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Setter-based Injection:"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "java",
          "code": "@Component\npublic class OrderService {\n    private PaymentService paymentService;\n\n    @Autowired\n    public void setPaymentService(PaymentService paymentService) {\n        this.paymentService = paymentService;\n    }\n}",
          "runnable": false
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 14,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "5-optionally-integrate-with-spring-boot-for-simplicity",
      "heading": "5. Optionally Integrate with Spring Boot for Simplicity",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Spring Boot makes bootstrapping Spring applications much easier by:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Eliminating the need for boilerplate XML",
            "Enabling embedded servers like Tomcat",
            "Providing auto-configuration",
            "Offering built-in monitoring and production-readiness features"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Spring Boot Example:"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "java",
          "code": "@SpringBootApplication\npublic class MyApp {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        SpringApplication.run(MyApp.class, args);\n    }\n}",
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Dependencies via Maven Starter:"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "language": "xml",
          "code": "<dependency>\n  <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n  <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-web</artifactId>\n</dependency>",
          "runnable": false
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 35,
      "subsections": []
    }
